                <pb facs="1060" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Robertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-10T15:00:00-05:00">December 10,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1965. Chungking report appearing Dec 9 papers here states <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >inter alia</hi> that Chinese have obtained Russian permission to occupy
                    Harbin, Changchun and Dairen.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report urgently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
